<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantin von Kaufmann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818–1882</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Konstantin Petrovich von Kaufmann</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantin von Kaufmann was a Russian general and the first governor-general of Russian Turkestan, from its creation in 1867 until his death in 1882. From <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> he directed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in 1868, made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a> after campaigns in 1868 and 1873, and annexed the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a> in 1876. He ruled the region with wide powers and encouraged trade and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> growing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstantin-von-kaufmann.jpg" alt="Konstantin von Kaufmann" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Рисовал К. О. Брож, гравировал Л. А. Серяков · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Von_Kaufman_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
